# Upstream files this integration deliberately does not ship.
#
# Intentionally empty.
#
# This used to list public/website/ — the standalone pharmacy marketing site,
# which routes/web.php answered / with, so the application presented a second
# website next to TIBADesk-website. It was deleted so a sync could not put that
# back.
#
# It is now shipped again and routed nowhere. The decision is upstream files are
# never deleted: a module that drops its author's files cannot be diffed back
# against the source it came from, and "that file is gone" is not a thing you
# want to discover after the fact.
#
# What keeps a second website off the screen is not deletion but routing:
# packages/tibadesk-overlay/pharmacy/routes/web.php is the overlay's own, and its
# catch-all sends an unmatched path to the panel rather than to a website. So
# public/website/ is inert. It is reachable as static files under /website/ only
# if the web server is left to serve public/ directly, which is the archived copy
# of the original site, not a front door.
#
# If you ever need a path deleted here, list it one per line below. Paths are
# relative to the application root and are checked by bin/sync-apps.sh --verify.
# Blank lines and # comments are ignored.
#
# Note that public/dashboard/ is not a candidate and is not listed. It is the
# panel's own built SPA — the interface a pharmacy uses once signed in — and it is
# absent from this repository's source tree as editable React, so it is shipped
# pre-built and must stay.
